 r←Test_Misc_026(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;a;b;c;beta1;beta2
⍝ Exercise `Registry.IsLaterThan`, which decides whether a Registry offers something later than
⍝ what is installed. Answering "different" instead of "later" once reported a downgrade as an update.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 (a b c)←'aplteam-Foo-1.1.0' 'aplteam-Foo-1.2.0' 'aplteam-Foo-2.0.0'
 (beta1 beta2)←'aplteam-Foo-1.2.0-beta-1' 'aplteam-Foo-1.2.0-beta-2'

⍝ Ordinary version numbers
 →T.PassesIf 1=b Reg.IsLaterThan a
 →T.PassesIf 0=a Reg.IsLaterThan b
 →T.PassesIf 0=a Reg.IsLaterThan a
 →T.PassesIf 1=c Reg.IsLaterThan b

⍝ Double digits must not be compared as text
 →T.PassesIf 1='aplteam-Foo-1.10.0'Reg.IsLaterThan'aplteam-Foo-1.9.0'

⍝ A beta comes before the release it leads up to, and after the version before it
 →T.PassesIf 1=b Reg.IsLaterThan beta2
 →T.PassesIf 0=beta2 Reg.IsLaterThan b
 →T.PassesIf 1=beta1 Reg.IsLaterThan a
 →T.PassesIf 0=a Reg.IsLaterThan beta1

⍝ This is what the bug was: what a Registry offers may be earlier than what is installed
 →T.PassesIf 0='aplteam-APLGit2-1.1.0'Reg.IsLaterThan'aplteam-APLGit2-1.2.0-beta-2'

 r←T._OK
⍝Done
